  "output": "out",
  "lights_contract": "Lights come from the Lights parameter of the render that draws the glass (in the demo, the Render Pass TOP 'render'). TouchDesigner recompiles the material per light setup: TD_NUM_LIGHTS Light COMPs go through TDLightingPBR() (point, cone, distant, attenuation, shadows); TD_NUM_ENV_LIGHTS Environment Light COMPs go through TDEnvLightTextureLod() for reflections and TDEnvLightingPBR() for ambient; Ambient Light COMPs arrive in uTDGeneral.ambientColor. With none of a kind, Auto falls back to the built-in key light or studio.",
  "coordinate_contract": "World-space normals, eye vector and lighting (GLSL MAT Lighting Space = World Space); camera-space refraction offset projected with the camera's own projection; screen UV from gl_FragCoord and uTDGeneral.viewport; environment direction = uTDEnvLights[i].rotate * world direction; object-space liquid noise.",
  "color_contract": "Colour parameters are artistic values passed as data vectors (no colour-space conversion). Light and environment values arrive as TouchDesigner computes them. Output is premultiplied alpha; the material blends with One / One Minus Source Alpha. The shader never calls TDDither (continuous output).",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "target_build": "Inspect host; written for TouchDesigner 2025.x (GLSL 4.60), not yet run natively",
  "derived_from": {
    "study": "studies/liquid-glass",
    "commit": "a6f95c6"
  },
  "external_dependencies": [],
  "native_status": "pending: not compiled or rendered in TouchDesigner yet; see validation.json",
  "integration_contract": "The glass joins a scene through a Render Pass TOP built on the scene's Render TOP, keeping its colour and depth, so opaque objects in front of the glass stay in front. The Refraction TOP is that same scene render: a 2D render (Render Mode 2D) from one camera, at the glass render's resolution. The demo follows this recipe: demo_scene (backdrop card, optional occluder) -> render (Render Pass TOP with the glass)."
